# global_access.tkr — §15 `global`, the no-namespace-qualifier access modifier, exercised end to end:
# a `global fn`/`type` reached bare from another namespace, the qualified path still valid (additive), a
# cross-namespace global overload selected by signature, `exp`+`global` composing, and an
# `exp global comptime` folding. One witness number only the correct resolution produces:
#   ping()=7 + a::ping()=7 + Tag{n=5}.n=5 + f(10)=10 + f(1,2)=3 + g()=3 + a::cz_probe()=4 = 39.
# A relapse in any access path moves the total off 39.

Feature: global_access — a `global` declaration is reachable without its namespace, additively

  Scenario: bare + qualified + global-overload + exp/comptime composition all reach the right bodies
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "39"
